Z||000016||JayUSA77||08-22-2001||10:30 PM||||ya it did have to be grounded to work, thanks tigger!! now where should i mount this damn thing? i put is on the closest piece of metal but its highly visable.<BR>HMMM another bump in the road. oh well im not mad at least they work.<BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000017||Tigger||08-22-2001||10:54 PM||||The relay on mine is located about 4" above and 5" or so behind the light for the footwell, it's tucked up behind the dash pretty good.  You might need to get another sheetmetal grounding screw for it.<P>Thanks, glad I could help out!||||reg||7
Z||000018||mbramble||08-23-2001||07:19 AM||||There is a hole for mounting it above the ground screw shown in one of the photos above.  It is up several inches and more toward the front of the car on that sidewall.  Move that sound deadening material around and you should find the hole.||||reg||1
